  "note": "Parliamentary republic with a collegial executive. Two Captains Regent, elected by the Grand and General Council every six months and invested on 1 April and 1 October, are joint heads of state. The Congress of State (government) answers to the Council; its Secretary of State for Foreign and Political Affairs is treated here as head of government. Modelled as 'parliamentary' rather than 'directorial' because the government depends on a Council majority."
